  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Suramin is an antiprotozoal drug used against trypanosomiasis, and has also been studied as an antineoplastic and antinematodal agent. It is listed as investigational in DrugBank and has no European Union authorisation, though it appears on the WHO essential medicines list.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q425946&quot;>Wikidata Q425946</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>suramin sodium</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>P01CX02</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB04786&quot;>DB04786</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/5361&quot;>5361</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:45906&quot;>45906</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q425946&quot;>Q425946</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C51H40N6O23S6</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>1297.26 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
